---
import Article from "../../../layouts/Article.astro";
import KeyTakeaway from "../../../components/KeyTakeaway.astro";
import InfoBox from "../../../components/InfoBox.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../../../components/ComparisonTable.astro";
import GiftPick from "../../../components/GiftPick.astro";
---

<Article
  title="Catan Gift Ideas: 10 Gifts for Catan Players (2026)"
  description="Gifts for someone who loves Catan: 3D-printed resource tokens, a robber upgrade, Longest Road and Largest Army trophies, a handmade Catan blanket, and STL files for 3D printers."
  game="catan"
  gameTitle="Catan"
  category="Guide"
  publishDate="2026-10-09"
>
  <p>
    Almost every board-game shelf has a copy of Catan, which makes it one of the
    easiest games to shop for. Whoever you're buying for already plays it, so the
    best gifts make the games they already play look and feel better, or settle
    the arguments it's famous for. Here are ten, from stocking stuffers to the one
    the whole table will fight over.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="The best gift for a Catan player is 3D-printed resource tokens: they replace the cards everyone handles all game. For a small gift, Longest Road and Largest Army trophies or a robber upgrade are hard to beat, and the handmade Catan blanket is the big one for a true fan." />

  <h2>The upgrade the whole table uses</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-resource-tokens"
    label="Our top pick"
    note="Little wood logs, bricks, sheep, wheat and ore to replace the resource cards. Trades get faster, new players follow along more easily, and the table looks like the island it represents."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="hexagon-token-trays"
    note="Stackable hex bowls to keep those resources sorted on the table. A natural add-on if you're buying the tokens."
  />

  <h2>Small gifts that settle arguments</h2>
  <p>
    Catan players argue about who has Longest Road and who's really winning.
    These end the discussion and make great stocking stuffers.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-trophies"
    label="Best small gift"
    note="Physical trophies for Longest Road and Largest Army, plus a Snail Award for the slowest player. They move around the table as the game swings."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-score-tracker"
    note="A victory point board that keeps everyone's score visible, for 4- and 6-player games. No more recounting at the end."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-robber-upgrade"
    note="A thief figure carrying stolen sheep and wood, to replace the plain grey robber. Rolling a 7 never looked this good."
  />

  <h2>For the person who always wins</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-trophy"
    note="The Ruler of Catan trophy, for whoever wins game night. Hand it over at the end of each game and watch the rivalry grow."
  />

  <h2>For a tidier table</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-player-tray"
    note="A player tray with a built-in card holder: resources, development cards and pieces in one place. Buy one per regular player."
  />

  <h2>The big gift for a true fan</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-blanket"
    label="Handmade"
    note="A crocheted hexagon throw inspired by the island of Catan, made by hand. Cosy gamer decor for game night on the sofa."
  />

  <h2>For the friend with a 3D printer</h2>
  <p>
    If they print their own upgrades, give them the files. They're instant
    downloads, so there's no shipping to wait for.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-player-tray-stl"
    note="Print-at-home files for our Catan player tray. One download, as many trays as the table needs, in any colour."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="catan-score-tracker-stl"
    note="The score tracker as print files, for 4- and 6-player games."
  />

  <h2>Which Catan gift fits?</h2>

  <ComparisonTable>
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">If they…</th>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Give them</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Play Catan every game night</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Resource tokens</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Need a small or stocking gift</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Longest Road & Largest Army trophies</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Always argue about the score</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Score tracker</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Are the group's champion</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Ruler of Catan trophy</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Are a true superfan</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Handmade Catan blanket</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Own a 3D printer</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Player tray or score tracker STL files</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ComparisonTable>

  <InfoBox type="tip" title="Want to give them more Catan?">
    If they've played the base game to death, an expansion is the other classic
    Catan gift. Our <a href="/games/catan/best-expansions-ranked/">Catan expansions, ranked</a>
    guide explains which one suits which group.
  </InfoBox>

  <InfoBox type="warning" title="Order a little earlier than usual">
    Everything here is made to order in our workshop in Sweden and shipped from
    there. Check the delivery estimate on the Etsy listing before you order, and
    give yourself a few extra days in December.
  </InfoBox>

  <p>
    Shopping for more than one gamer? Our
    <a href="/gifts/">gift guide for board gamers</a> covers other games, handmade
    pieces and gifts for every budget.
  </p>
</Article>
